Flecha: a shortcut with Option matches the key Option was held on.

Chromium names a key by the character it types (KeyboardCodeFromNSEvent),
and Option changes that character. On US International, Option-N types "~",
so Cmd-Option-N reached the focus manager as Cmd-Option-grave: Flecha's
Cmd-Option-N (new Flechinha) never matched, and the main menu then took the
"~" as Cmd-Shift-grave (Previous Window). Flecha's shortcuts name the key
itself, as the shortcut recorder in Settings does.

When nothing took the key as typed, prePerformKeyEquivalent: asks again with
the character typed without Option (charactersIgnoringModifiers, so Dvorak
and other layouts still name their own keys) and runs the Flecha shortcut
for it in that window, a Settings popup too. DispatchFlechaShortcut() is the
flechaPrivate.onShortcut dispatch of the shell's frame, for any window.

